# "Gain control of target permanent you own but don't control": with two of Bot1's Moxen in Bot2's hands (Pearl, Jet - two Harmless Offerings, on turns 1 and 3) the attack trigger asks for a choice among
# exactly those two. Bot1's own Mox Ruby (it controls it) and Bot2's own Ornithopter (it owns it) are refused; Bot1 takes the Jet back and Bot2 keeps the Pearl.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Coveted Falcon
Harmless Offering
Harmless Offering
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Coveted Falcon.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Harmless Offering.Cast
Bot1.Target(Bot2)
Bot1.Target(Mox Pearl)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Harmless Offering.Cast
Bot1.Target(Bot2)
Bot1.Target(Mox Jet)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield = Ornithopter; Mox Pearl; Mox Jet
Bot1.Attack(Coveted Falcon > Bot2)
! Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby)
! Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot2.Battlefield = Ornithopter; Mox Pearl
Bot1.Battlefield = Coveted Falcon; Mox Ruby; Mox Sapphire; Mox Jet
